<div class="page">
  <div class="running-head">150 Moallem and Boal</div>
  <div class="page-number">{{ page_number_150 }}</div>
  <p>be gauged by comparing "On the Pulse of Morning" with the poem read</p>
  <p>on an earlier such occasion—Robert Frost's "The Gift Outright," deliv</p>
  <p>ered in January 1961 at Kennedy's inauguration.</p>
  <p>The land was ours before we were the land's.</p>
  <p>She was our land more than a hundred years</p>
  <p>ago. She was our land, she was ours</p>
  <p>in Massachusetts, in Virginia,</p>
  <p>but we were England's, still colonial,</p>
  <p>possessing what we still were unpossessed by.</p>
  <p>Something we were, something we were possessed.</p>
  <p>Something we were withholding made us weak</p>
  <p>until we found it out was ourselves</p>
  <p>We were withholding from our land of living,</p>
  <p>And forthwith found salvation in surrender.</p>
  <p>Such as we were gave ourselves outright</p>
  <p>(The deed of gift was many years of dawn)</p>
  <p>To the land vaguely realizing westward,</p>
  <p>Such as she was, such as she would become.</p>
</div>

