  <p>the histories of colonialism and anti-imperialism (Barnett 1993). The</p>
  <p>history of colonialism is a history of domination, and the history of</p>
  <p>domination is a history of the construction of difference. The</p>
  <p>construction of difference is the process by which we make one</p>
  <p>group different from another, and this process is always</p>
  <p>accompanied by the construction of hierarchy. The concept of</p>
  <p>difference, in this sense, is not merely a descriptive category</p>
  <p>but a political one, a category that is always implicated in</p>
